# Storacha Authentication - Choose ONE of the following approaches:

# Approach 1: Direct credentials (from w3 CLI export)
# STORACHA_KEY=MgCYuJF7...your-private-key...
# STORACHA_PROOF=uuYAIJlY...your-proof-delegation...

# Approach 2: UCAN file (generated with w3 CLI)
# STORACHA_UCAN_FILE=./my-ucan.car

# Approach 3: UCAN token (base64 encoded)
# STORACHA_UCAN_TOKEN=base64-encoded-ucan-token

# Alternative environment variable names (also supported)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STORACHA_PRIVATE_KEY=MgCYuJF7...
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STORACHA_DELEGATION=uuYAIJlY...
# W3_PRINCIPAL=MgCYuJF7...
# W3_PROOF=uuYAIJlY...
# W3_UCAN_FILE=./my-ucan.car
# W3_UCAN_TOKEN=base64-encoded-token

# ── Pinata (backend driver, #54 phase 0.5.3) ─────────────────────────────
#
# Use a SCOPED key, never an admin key: an admin key is the whole account, and
# this one lives in a .env on a development machine and in CI.
#
# The conformance suite exercises all four operations a driver declares, so the
# key needs upload, pin-by-CID, list and delete. A write-only key does not fail
# gracefully — the driver would declare `listing: true` and then not be able to,
# which is exactly the mismatch `checkBackend` exists to prevent.
#
# PINATA_JWT=eyJhbGciOi...your-scoped-key...
#
# The dedicated gateway to retrieve through, without a scheme —
# `something.mypinata.cloud`. Retrieval by CID also works through the public
# gateways, but a dedicated one is not rate-limited against everyone else.
#
# PINATA_GATEWAY=your-gateway.mypinata.cloud
